From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:04:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): validate review handoffs and accept
 legacy automatic class routing

Problem: class:deep/board-default handoffs were persisted successfully but
review dispatch rejected them before spawning.
Root (happened): ingress and dispatch had inconsistent metadata contracts.
Root (not caught): validation ran only after the durable review transition;
existing tests exercised bad metadata only at dispatch.
Recurrence: searched current main history and PRs for review board-default;
no prior compatibility fix found.

Share the override parser between ingress and dispatch. Only the historical
board-default sentinel on class selectors aliases auto; concrete/unknown
providers paired with class selectors remain rejected. Refuse invalid
handoffs before artifact handling or task/run/event mutation. Preserve
existing override precedence, registry checks and independent fallback.
Move unchanged review redaction helper into the topical module, retaining
its kanban_db import alias to respect the facade size ratchet.

Proof: new regression suite RED 7 failed/2 passed on unchanged source;
GREEN 264 tests across seven review/managed-policy/tool-contract suites,
zero failures. scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks passed.
Historical invalid-metadata dispatcher tests now seed persisted fixtures
directly, preserving fail-closed coverage after ingress refusal.
